#### Example 2: Extension .npmrc Configuration by IP Classification

```ini
# .npmrc for Gainwell-Owned Extension (Full Access)
@gainwell:registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/gainwell/_packaging/gainwell-design-system/npm/registry/
always-auth=true
//pkgs.dev.azure.com/gainwell/_packaging/gainwell-design-system/npm/registry/:username=gainwell
//pkgs.dev.azure.com/gainwell/_packaging/gainwell-design-system/npm/registry/:_password=${GAINWELL_NPM_TOKEN}
//pkgs.dev.azure.com/gainwell/_packaging/gainwell-design-system/npm/registry/:email=npm@gainwell.com
```

```ini
# .npmrc for State-Exclusive Extension (Public Access Only)
@gainwell:registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/gainwell/_packaging/gainwell-design-system/npm/registry/
always-auth=true
//pkgs.dev.azure.com/gainwell/_packaging/gainwell-design-system/npm/registry/:username=texas-medicaid
//pkgs.dev.azure.com/gainwell/_packaging/gainwell-design-system/npm/registry/:_password=${STATE_NPM_TOKEN}
//pkgs.dev.azure.com/gainwell/_packaging/gainwell-design-system/npm/registry/:email=texas@gainwell.com

# Restrict to public package only
package-lock=false  # Prevent accidental partner package installation
```

